{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1232694-otherwordly-demesne-and-hallows","id":1232694,"title":"Otherwordly Demesne and Hallows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-05T13:54:27-07:00","id":1232694,"title":"Otherwordly Demesne and Hallows","content":"I was thinking... <br /> in the mage corebook nothing says that a<br /> Demesne must be created ONLY in the material world. <br /> Do you think a mage could open a Shadow Demesne? Or one in the Temenos? <br /> <br /> And what about Supernal Verges and Hallows, do you think they may manifest in other realms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T14:10:59-07:00","id":1232699,"title":"","content":"Yep, I'm fairly certain all of these things are possible.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't allow it in a Lower Depth, but any part of the Fallen World (Underworld, Shadow, Hedge, Astral, etc) would be fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T15:07:18-07:00","id":1232718,"title":"","content":"In a sense a Mage\u2019s Oneiros already functions as an Astral demesne since it\u2019s Paradox free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T16:31:35-07:00","id":1232742,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the main trouble with otherworldly Demesnes is just that there isn't as much of a <i>point</i> to them \u2014 the existing Paradox reduction for the primary otherworlds and the fact that a Demesne only offers its benefits to spells that suit its semiotics means you're often going to be better-served setting up your dedicated ritual space in the material world where you don't have to set up spells allowing you to cross dimensions to be able to make use of it.<br /> <br /> Supernal Verges can show up theoretically anywhere, but given the universal tendency of Hallows to form near significant and unique features I wouldn't imagine they're likely to show up in other worlds except in the sense of normal geographical overlap like that found in the Shadow or the Anima Mundi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T23:03:48-07:00","id":1232805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1232694-otherwordly-demesne-and-hallows?p=1232742#post1232742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the main trouble with otherworldly Demesnes is just that there isn't as much of a <i>point</i> to them \u2014 the existing Paradox reduction for the primary otherworlds and the fact that a Demesne only offers its benefits to spells that suit its semiotics means you're often going to be better-served setting up your dedicated ritual space in the material world where you don't have to set up spells allowing you to cross dimensions to be able to make use of it.<br /> <br /> Supernal Verges can show up theoretically anywhere, but given the universal tendency of Hallows to form near significant and unique features I wouldn't imagine they're likely to show up in other worlds except in the sense of normal geographical overlap like that found in the Shadow or the Anima Mundi.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is true but the primary otherworlds only reduces the paradox rolls of the corresponding Arcana of 2 dice, a mage could build a Safe place in the Shadow casting the spell Spirit manse and gain greater bonuses also opening a Demesne in this personal reign (summoning supernal entities, astral entry point, greater paradox reduction and yantra bonus for some spells ). <br /> <br /> For otherwordly Hallows my greater doubt is that major Hallows are also Nodes and i don t know if Ley Lines could manifest in non material realms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 07-06-2018, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T01:07:02-07:00","id":1232818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1232694-otherwordly-demesne-and-hallows?p=1232805#post1232805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is true but the primary otherworlds only reduces the paradox rolls of the corresponding Arcana of 2 dice, a mage could build a Safe place in the Shadow casting the spell Spirit manse and gain greater bonuses also opening a Demesne in this personal reign (summoning supernal entities, astral entry point, greater paradox reduction and yantra bonus for some spells ).<br /> <br /> For otherwordly Hallows my greater doubt is that major Hallows are also Nodes and i don t know if Ley Lines could manifest in non material realms</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally they don't have to be the same. Nothing says a Demense in the Underworld (which has a reduction for Death Paradoxs) can't be Mind aspected or one in the Shadow can't be aligned with Matter.<br /> <br /> Hollows produce Mana, they are worth a short otherworldly jaunt because of that alone, but if you have a Mystery there as well, they can become a kind of base camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}